commit ae61cdb82d0e753a34851c7ce0b4ce532ad71514
Author: Ritesh Talwadekar <[REDACTED-EMAIL]>
Date:   Mon Sep 14 22:56:59 2026 +0100

    fix(ops,ingest): Task 137 -- overnight continuity, scope accuracy, delivery fairness
    
    Five concrete findings from Task 136's evidence review, each investigated
    and closed with a bounded, demonstrated fix:
    
    1. EOD "PARTIAL" status is a standing, permanent condition for this
       deployment (piv_paper is intentionally never checked -- PIV/Alpaca is
       opt-in-only and never wired up), not evidence of a real problem, so
       eod_reconciled_today could never become true here even on a fully
       correct, on-time reconciliation. New talonx_ops.eod_reconciliation.
       reconciled_to_available_scope() distinguishes "PARTIAL solely because
       piv_paper is NOT_CHECKED, no mismatches, everything else CHECKED" from
       a genuinely broken/incomplete reconciliation -- exposed as a SEPARATE,
       explicitly-named signal (eod_reconciled_today_available_scope /
       today_reconciled_available_scope) in supervisor.py and authoritative_
       read_model.py, never silently reclassifying the existing strict field.
    
    2. Deferred-lookup SATURATION (not merely "one failing row doesn't stop
       the rest of an already-selected batch", already covered): reproduced
       with a bounded selection `limit` entirely filled by rows whose lookup
       always raises -- a valid, eligible row sitting behind them in band/
       enqueue order was never selected at all, on any cycle. Fixed: a DEFER
       outcome now writes a bounded, fixed backoff (_DEFER_BACKOFF_SECONDS=
       30s) to the row's own next_retry_at_utc -- the SAME column/mechanism
       pending() already filters on -- so a permanently-failing row stops
       monopolizing its slot after a short window, while `state` itself is
       never touched (not terminal, fully recoverable, exactly-once on
       success). The bulk expire_stale() sweep deliberately does NOT filter
       on next_retry_at_utc itself (that column is shared with the UNRELATED
       send-attempt backoff mark_failed() sets; filtering the age sweep on it
       would let a row merely awaiting a send retry escape an age expiry it
       still needs) -- it still benefits by writing the same backoff if it
       reaches a failing row first.
    
    3. Scope reporting was narrower than actual runtime evaluation: the
       observational V2 near-miss funnel (talonx_ops/prospective/funnel.py)
       independently recomputed a ~39-issuer (watchlist-only) execution scope
       for its own Form 4/code-P/cluster analysis, while the LIVE V2 companion
       (talonx_v2/run.py --enable-broad-discovery) actually evaluates the
       union with the frozen 626-name Discovery Universe v1 manifest --
       confirmed genuinely wider runtime evaluation, narrow REPORTING only.
       funnel.build_funnel() gains include_broad_discovery, unioning in the
       SAME manifest talonx_v2/run.py uses and reporting BOTH the resolved
       and watchlist-only counts, explicitly labelled (never silently
       substituting one for the other). checkpoint.py's capture() determines
       whether to pass it from the LIVE companion's own reported execution_
       scope_count (v2_service_status.json), never a hardcoded assumption.
    
    4. Original ("V1") strategy fingerprint mismatch (2dea67a6f6d2 vs
       expected 2ae6216bca70) fully traced per-file/per-commit: TWO distinct
       causes, not one. (a) line-ending representation -- the working tree
       materialises the 5 fingerprinted files with CRLF (Windows checkout);
       the committed git blobs are pure LF -- fixed by LF-normalizing before
       hashing in get_strategy_version() (talonx_backtest/reproducibility.py),
       the same technique tests/test_task65b_protected_fingerprints.py
       already uses for two other frozen fingerprints. (b) a REAL, substantive,
       already-authorized change: commit 66a49f9 (Task 135, same session)
       modified talonx_quant/consumer.py -- one of the 5 fingerprinted files
       -- after the constant was frozen; that commit's own message incorrectly
       claimed no fingerprinted file was touched. Not reverted (legitimate,
       tested, already-pushed) -- confined to Pub/Sub delivery-observability
       logging/metrics around an already-decided signal publish, not gating/
       scoring logic. V1_FINGERPRINT_EXPECTED corrected to the new, current,
       LF-normalized, reproducible-from-git baseline: ed8272fe568d.
    
    5. The 35 real FAILED_RETRYABLE rows rejected for "token:buy" are 100%
       one issuer (BBY / Best Buy Co Inc) across every filing type --
       conclusively a deterministic classification false positive, not a
       transient failure: the company's own factual, SEC-sourced name
       contains the literal word "Buy". claim_safety.scan_rendered/
       assert_clean gain an optional company_name exemption (threaded through
       from enqueue_card's already-available card.company_name) that excludes
       only bare buy/sell tokens that are part of the filer's own known name
       string -- every other rule, including phrase-level predictive language
       ("strong buy", "should buy") and unrelated bare tokens, is completely
       unaffected. No global content-guard relaxation.
    
    Also investigated and traced (evidence-only, no code change needed):
    LULU pre-enqueue latency (accession 0001397187-26-000129) -- enrichment
    (sub-second, 20:18:30-31Z) and delivery (~8-9s to send) are precisely
    measured with no defect; the source-to-local-discovery interval (SEC
    accepted 16:15:47Z -> our poller) cannot be precisely localized --
    `ingested_at_utc`/`enqueued_at_utc` is confirmed BATCH-fixed (shared
    across many unrelated records, not a true per-record marker); the best
    available circumstantial evidence (poll-cycle `filings=` counter
    increments) points to a poll cycle completing ~20:18:31Z, ~4h after SEC
    acceptance, but the true cause (SEC-side propagation lag vs our own
    scheduling) cannot be determined from available evidence -- reported as
    an explicit gap, not invented.
    
    19 new/updated focused tests (test_task137_overnight_continuity.py new;
    test_delivery_claim_safety.py +5; test_backtest_reproducibility.py +1;
    test_task114_prospective.py fingerprint assertion now reads the live
    constant instead of a duplicated stale literal; test_task136b_freshness_
    edge_cases.py 2 assertions updated for the new DEFER-backoff timing).
    575 tests pass across every directly affected module; 11 pre-existing,
    unrelated failures reconfirmed present on unmodified HEAD (environmental
    live-process-scan refusals + date-dependent fixtures), none caused by
    this change.
    
    Frozen V2 fingerprint 11107198c5b81237 unchanged and re-verified. No
    strategy/gating/scoring logic touched anywhere in this change.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

